# Nonsecret release coordinates for a Linux Weles deployment.
#
# `scripts/chromium/download.sh` refuses to install anything without an exact
# version and digest, which is the point: the fingerprint patches in the Weles
# Chromium build are what make a login survive a bot check, so a host may not
# substitute a distro or snap browser. A candidate host that carries no
# deployment env yet is told the coordinates with this file, delivered through
# `stado host install-file <host> … weles-release-coordinates.env`, and read by
# the checked-in helpers -- never as an argument on anybody's command line.
#
# The version is the one charless-mac-mini runs today, measured from its own
# deployment env. The digest is PER ARCHIVE, so the value here is the digest of
# the linux-amd64 archive and is deliberately empty until that archive is
# published: an installer given the darwin digest would fail its checksum, and an
# installer given no digest refuses, which is the correct behaviour when the
# platform's release does not exist yet.
WELES_CHROMIUM_RELEASE_VERSION=147.0.7727.108-weles.1
WELES_CHROMIUM_RELEASE_SHA256=
WELES_RELEASE_PLATFORM=linux-amd64
